	shorttitle = {Unveiling specialisation trends in economics research},
	abstract = {Fields of study have become more specialised over time. Within fields, divisions between empirical/applied and theoretical branches have also emerged. This column uses a large corpus of economics research articles to analyse long-term trends in citations and methodological strategies. Since the 1990s, there has been a relative decline in theory articles and an increase in applied and applied theory research in economics. Trends for theory and econometric methods articles – including the breadth of topics covered and extramural citations and references – suggest greater specialisation. Meanwhile, applied economics research appears to have become more multidisciplinary over the past 50 years.},
